course: dictionary
lesson: 10603
title: Undissolved: still there, not mixed in
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Dissolve means to mix into a liquid so completely that it disappears. The start of the word, un-, means not, so undissolved means not dissolved: the solid is still there, still solid, and not mixed in. «Filtering separates an undissolved solid from a liquid.» The clues are separates, solid and liquid, so the solid stays as a solid while the liquid passes through.
explain: Picture stirring sugar into water. If grains are still lying at the bottom after a long stir, they are undissolved. Check it by swapping your meaning into the sentence: «A filter separates a solid that is still solid from a liquid» makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Why does a solid stay undissolved? Sometimes the liquid is full, so it cannot hold any more (we say it is saturated). Sometimes the solid will never dissolve, like sand in water. Either way, the solid stays undissolved.
fact: Undissolved means not dissolved: still solid in a liquid.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so «undissolved» means «not dissolved».
fact: «Undissolved sugar» is sugar still visible at the bottom after stirring.
fact: A solid stays undissolved when the liquid is saturated (can't hold any more) or when the solid is insoluble, like sand.
fact: Undissolved solids can be separated from a liquid by filtering.
exercise: «Filtering separates an undissolved solid from a liquid.» What does undissolved mean here? | Frozen into ice | Coloured bright red | Fully mixed in and gone | *Still solid, not mixed in
exercise: Maya stirs sugar into her tea and some grains stay at the bottom. Which word describes those grains? | Melted | Evaporated | Dissolved | *Undissolved
exercise: Find and copy the word that means not dissolved in «A filter separates an undissolved solid from a liquid.» | *undissolved | liquid | filter | separates
test: Why does sand stay undissolved in water? | Because the water is boiling | *Because sand is insoluble and will not dissolve | Because sand is a liquid | Because the sand has disappeared
test: Which process separates an undissolved solid from a liquid? | Stirring | Melting | Freezing | *Filtering
exam: Which sentence uses undissolved correctly? | Undissolved is the colour of the sea | The water undissolved the sugar in one minute | *Some salt stayed undissolved at the bottom of the glass | The salt was undissolved and vanished completely
